Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:56:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 21/52] Run the latest VitaAutotests, and fix some thread and
 callback behavior found (#4236)

* ci: run the latest VitaAutotests

Move AUTOTESTS_REF to the VitaAutotests commit that adds 47 more tests,
and give each of them its outcome on Vita3K in expectations.txt. Four
of them pass, the others fail, crash or time out on what each line
says. The runner now finds tests by their .expected files, since the
suite also has the source of a module under tests/.

* cpu: handle TPIDRURW

User code may read and write TPIDRURW with MRC and MCR, but Vita3K
only handled TPIDRURO, so the JIT asserted on the first access.
TPIDRURW now has its own value per thread. It is 0 when a thread
starts, also when it starts again, and the thread gets its own value
back after a callback. _sceKernelGetThreadContextForVM reports it
instead of TPIDRURO.

* kernel: start threads and callbacks with the VFP state of a Vita

Threads started with FPSCR 0, where a Vita starts every thread with
0x03000000, round to nearest with flush-to-zero and default NaN. A
callback ran with the thread's FPSCR and VFP exception setting, where
on a Vita it starts with those of a new thread and the thread gets its
own back after it. The other guest calls Vita3K makes from HLE code,
like library callbacks, keep the caller's state as before.

* kernel: fix thread signal timeouts and targets

sceKernelWaitSignal ignored its timeout and waited until a signal came,
and sceKernelSendSignal used the target without checking it, so a
signal to a UID that isn't a thread crashed Vita3K. A wait now ends
with WAIT_TIMEOUT when its timeout passes, writes back the time left
when it waited, and leaves the timeout alone when a signal was already
there. A signal to UID 0 fails with ILLEGAL_THREAD_ID and one to what
isn't a thread with UNKNOWN_THREAD_ID, as on a Vita.

* kernel: check thread attributes and report them in thread info

sceKernelCreateThread took any attributes and thread info always
reported 0, and sceKernelChangeCurrentThreadAttr was unimplemented. A
Vita creates threads only with the attributes 0x2000, 0x01000000,
0x04000000 and 0x80000000, fails with ILLEGAL_ATTR for any other, and
reports the attributes given plus 0x80000000, which every user thread
has. sceKernelChangeCurrentThreadAttr takes only 0x01000000 and
0x80000000, and thread info doesn't show a change to either.

* kernel: leave TLS slot 0 at 0 for a new thread

Vita3K wrote 1 to TLS slot 0 as a stub process ID that nothing reads,
where a new thread on a Vita finds 0.

* kernel: report pending callbacks and clear taken callback arguments

Thread info always reported 0 in fNotifyCallback, where a Vita reports
1 for a waiting thread with a notified callback that hasn't run yet. A
callback that runs takes its notifications, and its info still showed
the last argument, where on a Vita it reads 0 like the count.

Each thread now counts its callbacks with notifications they haven't
run for, in place of the flag that woke its waits, so a callback that
was cancelled or deleted no longer counts as notified.

* kernel: delete a thread's callbacks when it ends

The callbacks a thread created outlived it, so another thread could
still notify and run them. On a Vita they go away when the thread ends,
whether it returns, exits or deletes itself, and their pending
notifications never run.

(cherry picked from commit 34566de6377723bf85f4570303b7293ebd37fd8d)
